   - n (total operators + operands): Indicates code size and complexity.
   - uniq_Op / uniq_Opnd (unique operators/operands): Diversity in operators and operands can highlight complexity.
   - t (time): Time required to comprehend the code; prolonged comprehension time can introduce errors.

3. Code count distributions:
   - loc (line count of code): Larger codebases have increased defect probabilities.
   - lOCode: Line of executable code; strongly correlates with defect density.
